{title: My Hope Is Built on Nothing Less}
{subtitle: The Solid Rock}
{lyricist: Edward Mote}
{composer: William B. Bradbury}
{year: 1834}
{meta: tune-year 1863}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune THE SOLID ROCK}
{meta: meter LM (8.8.8.8) with refrain}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to THE SOLID ROCK}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags hope, assurance}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My [D]hope is built on [G]nothing [D]less
Than [D]Jesus' blood and [E7]righteous[A]ness;
I [D]dare not trust the [G]sweetest [D]frame,
But [D]wholly [A]lean on [A7]Jesus' [D]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
On [D]Christ, the solid [G]Rock, I [D]stand;
All [G]other ground is [D]sinking sand,
All [D]other ground is [A7]sinking [D]sand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When [D]darkness veils His [G]lovely [D]face,
I [D]rest on His un[E7]changing [A]grace;
In [D]every high and [G]stormy [D]gale,
My [D]anchor [A]holds with[A7]in the [D]veil.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
His [D]oath, His covenant, [G]His [D]blood
Sup[D]port me in the [E7]whelming [A]flood;
When [D]all around my [G]soul gives [D]way,
He [D]then is [A]all my [A7]hope and [D]stay.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
When [D]He shall come with [G]trumpet [D]sound,
O [D]may I then in [E7]Him be [A]found;
Dressed [D]in His righteous[G]ness a[D]lone,
Fault[D]less to [A]stand be[A7]fore the [D]throne.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
